From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: clear the suspending flag when the driver
 fails to suspend

__ieee80211_suspend() sets local->suspending and clears it only at the
end of a successful suspend. When drv_suspend() fails with a negative
error, the system suspend is aborted and the system keeps running, but
local->suspending stays set until the next successful suspend. In the
meantime ieee80211_mgd_probe_ap() takes every beacon loss for one during
a suspend and doesn't probe the AP, so a lost connection goes unnoticed.

Clear the flag on that error path too.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 net/mac80211/pm.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/mac80211/pm.c b/net/mac80211/pm.c
index f63676c44..c6dc494ad 100644
--- a/net/mac80211/pm.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/pm.c
@@ -118,6 +118,8 @@ int __ieee80211_suspend(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct cfg80211_wowlan *wowlan,
 		if (err < 0) {
 			local->quiescing = false;
 			local->wowlan = false;
+			/* the system stays up, see ieee80211_mgd_probe_ap() */
+			local->suspending = false;
 			if (ieee80211_hw_check(hw, AMPDU_AGGREGATION)) {
 				lockdep_assert_wiphy(local->hw.wiphy);
 				list_for_each_entry(sta,
